    "c5"
   ],
   "spoken": "A framing note before the theory: if you already have an answer to the London that makes you comfortable — a central strike, a fianchetto, whatever — keep playing it. What follows are proposals, not a demand to tear up a repertoire that already makes you happy."
  },
  {
   "ply": 5,
   "t": 2374.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp1ppppp/5n2/2P5/5B2/8/PPP1PPPP/RN1QKBNR b KQkq - 0 3",
   "line": [
    "dxc5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The opponent has a handful of tries against the early c-pawn break: an immediate capture, which is rare and simply not good; the ambitious central push to d5; the modest c3; and the topical e3. Knowing which is which is half the battle."
  },
