   "line": [
    "e3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Against the rare pawn-grab capture, the crisp reply is a knight to a6. If the queen recaptures, a check on a5 wins the pawn straight back, and keeping the queens on leads to a superior game with a better centre.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 3183.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp1ppppp/5n2/8/3p1B2/4P3/PPP2PPP/RN1QKBNR w KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "cxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now the topical main move — and the recommended treatment is to capture in the centre first and only then bring the queen to b6. Taking first is the point: it rules out an awkward queen retreat that would otherwise defend, since the pawn is left hanging, and it steers into a fresher position.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 3184.5,
   "fen": "rnb1kb1r/pp1ppppp/1q3n2/8/3P1B2/8/PPP2PPP/RN1QKBNR w KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "exd4",
    "Qb6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 5,
   "t": 3192,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp1ppppp/5n2/2p5/3P1B2/4P3/PPP2PPP/RN1QKBNR b KQkq - 0 3",
