   "line": [
    "b3"
   ],
   "spoken": "If the opponent props things with b3, nothing much happens — just answer with d5, and now the queenside light squares are permanently weakened, an inferior version of the main line for the first player.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 3468,
   "fen": "rnb1kb1r/pp2pppp/1q3n2/3p4/3P1B2/1P6/P1P2PPP/RN1QKBNR w KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 3476.5,
   "fen": "rnb1kb1r/pp2pppp/1q3n2/3p4/3P1B2/1P3N2/P1P2PPP/RN1QKB1R b KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The one rule always to remember here: a knight to f3 is met by the bishop pin to g4. Miss that chance and the natural developing move can allow an annoying central knight leap — so the pin comes first, every time.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
